{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen","id":1559346,"title":"Is Mage 5th edition going to happen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-11T03:39:00-07:00","id":1559346,"title":"Is Mage 5th edition going to happen?","content":"I've seen that there are some fifth edition books out for several years. Is Mage going to be part of that?<br /> <br /> I first got into <b>Mage </b>playing second edition <b>Ars Magica. </b>Although adore many White Wolf/Onyx Path games, I still love playing an Hermetic forty years on. Is <b>Mage </b>now over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T17:14:42-07:00","id":1559382,"title":"","content":"I know nothing of the inner workings of Paradox/White Wolf, but I imagine Bloodlines 2's failures have had some repercussions. I wouldn't be surprised if part of reason the White Wolf brand/division was revived was Paradox is looking for a buyer of the IP. If we do see White Wolf change hands, then I would suspect we would see Vampire 6th Edition first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-12T22:15:20-07:00","id":1559384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen#post1559346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen that there are some fifth edition books out for several years. Is Mage going to be part of that?<br /> <br /> I first got into <b>Mage </b>playing second edition <b>Ars Magica. </b>Although adore many White Wolf/Onyx Path games, I still love playing an Hermetic forty years on. Is <b>Mage </b>now over?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's safe to say the answer to that is 'no.'<br /> <br /> 5th edition vampire seems to be the only game line that's made any degree of success. Werewolf faired poorly, while Hunter was an even worse screw up. The Imbued aren't a thing anymore, which means all Hunters are just regular ass humans that are somehow immune to the effects of Delirium / The Mists for reasons that the authors couldn't be bothered to come with an explanation for.<br /> <br /> But not only that, 5th edition seems to be focused on dialing the power scale down to street level capabilities. Which is wholly counter intuitive to the entire premise of what Mage is all about. You're trying to achieve Ascension and become some kind of cosmic level being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-13T23:06:50-07:00","id":1559409,"title":"","content":"I've seen what I think may be part of the marketing on You Tube Shorts, an AI generated three minute blurb with the text it's based on being M20 info rewritten in to the same style V5, W5 and H5 the shorts use the still art is &quot;Urban Fantasy&quot; Wizards in the same art styles as used in the 5ed books seen all the Spheres Most of the Traditions and a couple of the Conventions.<br /> <br /> the Poster uses a series of Blind Accounts. some one may be testing the waters or if the project has gone under releasing unused marketing material hoping for the slim chance of a Revival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T11:22:42-07:00","id":1559432,"title":"","content":"Possibly not, to be candid im okay with that.<br /> <br /> From w5 and h5, m5 would just be a generic urban wizard game in a market saturated with them which would seriously damage it going forward.<br /> <br /> Id rather wait a few years and wait until the climates for likely to produce something good.<br /> <br /> I've done it before afterall with no hope of another edition back in the 00's afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T12:20:08-07:00","id":1559433,"title":"","content":"I've seen some information posted by former developers about things they've heard, and they didn't like much of it. Of course, this was about a year or so ago, so I don't know what the current status would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-15T19:51:12-07:00","id":1559442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559384#post1559384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5th edition vampire seems to be the only game line that's made any degree of success. Werewolf faired poorly, while Hunter was an even worse screw up.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Werewolf and Hunter never had the fan bases that Vampire and Mage have had. If <i>any</i> of the other WoD gamelines could achieve success comparable to V5, it would be Mage. Depending on how they do it, of course. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T02:24:45-07:00","id":1559447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559442#post1559442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Werewolf and Hunter never had the fan bases that Vampire and Mage have had. If <i>any</i> of the other WoD gamelines could achieve success comparable to V5, it would be Mage. Depending on how they do it, of course.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If they did it as a gritty street level game it would likely flop (although a gritty street level secret magic game might work, it wouldn't be Mage). <br /> <br /> Mage needs to be flexible enough to go from the streets to the stars and then off to fairyland or Indonesia. Mage needs to be multitudes of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-17T02:03:02-07:00","id":1559477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559442#post1559442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Werewolf and Hunter never had the fan bases that Vampire and Mage have had. If <i>any</i> of the other WoD gamelines could achieve success comparable to V5, it would be Mage. Depending on how they do it, of course.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, it could just be the fact that 5th edition is garbage, and the writers burned out their creative juices after making Vampire.<br /> <br /> Again, I'll point out the fact the Imbued are not a thing in 5th edition. Meaning that the hunters don't have divine protection, or the ability to shoot the holy fire out of their eyes, or whatever else they could previously do. They are just random citizens, plucked off the street who saw the monsters that lurk in the dark and decided to pick a fight.<br /> <br /> HOW do they not succumb to Delirium? Or have their memories wiped within hours of encountering a Fae?<br /> <br /> No idea! They're just inexplicably immune to such things. Clearly the answer can't be that they're secretly Kinfolk, because those don't exist anymore either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T20:02:35-07:00","id":1559514,"title":"","content":"God, I hope not. Everything from WoD5 gave me a bad taste in my mouth. Mage: The Ascension is my favorite World of Darkness gameline. I cannot imagine how awful a redux under Paradox's oversight would be.<br /> <br /> If M5 never happens, I'll be happy. Let's roll the dice that Paradox sells the property, and the next IP holder is more skittish about rocking the boat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T20:10:14-07:00","id":1559515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559442#post1559442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Werewolf and Hunter never had the fan bases that Vampire and Mage have had. If <i>any</i> of the other WoD gamelines could achieve success comparable to V5, it would be Mage. Depending on how they do it, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Hunter: The Reckoning had its own video games back during the original White Wolf era. So it can't have been that unpopular.<br /> <br /> But more to the point: W5 and H5 had the problem that they changed so much in a way that alienated its existing fanbase. Which is bad, when as you said those games didn't have a large following to begin with. V5 kind of got traction, because its fanbase is large enough that alienating part of it wasn't as big a kiss of death. (Though, it must be stressed, alienating the existing audience is NEVER a recipe for success within niche circles; they're the people who onboard new fans). W5 and H5 doubled down on changing their games and narrowing their scope - making shifts even V5 didn't do - at a time when they needed to preserve as many fans as possible.<br /> <br /> Like, Hunter: The Reckoning had cultivated its own group of folks who really liked the Imbued. And then H5 says &quot;actually no, forget all that&quot;. Anyone who was a fan of normal, lowercase-h hunters were either playing Hunters Hunted, or Hunter: The Vigil. You played Hunter: The Reckoning because you LIKED running characters with superpowers. Who exactly was H5 FOR?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-18T22:46:11-07:00","id":1559516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559515#post1559515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I e.<br /> <br /> Like, Hunter: The Reckoning had cultivated its own group of folks who really liked the Imbued. And then H5 says &quot;actually no, forget all that&quot;. Anyone who was a fan of normal, lowercase-h hunters were either playing Hunters Hunted, or Hunter: The Vigil. You played Hunter: The Reckoning because you LIKED running characters with superpowers. Who exactly was H5 FOR?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worse than that, at least V5 and W5 had to themselves the fact that they aere ttrpgs bout vampires and werewolves, which are pretty rare in terms both of ttrpgs and in general in IPs. If you speak of playing a vampire in both tabletop and video games, vtm will come to mind. And games bout plying werewolves aree even rarer.<br /> <br /> Now, playing humans hunting the supernatural? That's a dime a dozen in games. H5 was fighting everything from night's dark agents to the Dresden files ttrpg, hell, even modern day d20 is about that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T04:32:23-07:00","id":1559518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559516#post1559516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Worse than that, at least V5 and W5 had to themselves the fact that they aere ttrpgs bout vampires and werewolves, which are pretty rare in terms both of ttrpgs and in general in IPs. If you speak of playing a vampire in both tabletop and video games, vtm will come to mind. And games bout plying werewolves aree even rarer.<br /> <br /> Now, playing humans hunting the supernatural? That's a dime a dozen in games. H5 was fighting everything from night's dark agents to the Dresden files ttrpg, hell, even modern day d20 is about that</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the big problem I see with 5th ed mage, Hunter is so pointless that it may as well not exist mage if stripped of the settings depth will just be a generic urban wizard game in a market full of them.<br /> <br /> Then again paradox doesnt strictly speaking care about the core game so much as it's a platform to launch spin or build a franchise. Something painfully clear with werewolf and hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-19T04:37:15-07:00","id":1559519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559515#post1559515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But more to the point: W5 and H5 had the problem that they changed so much in a way that alienated its existing fanbase. Which is bad, when as you said those games didn't have a large following to begin with. V5 kind of got traction, because its fanbase is large enough that alienating part of it wasn't as big a kiss of death. (Though, it must be stressed, alienating the existing audience is NEVER a recipe for success within niche circles; they're the people who onboard new fans). W5 and H5 doubled down on changing their games and narrowing their scope - making shifts even V5 didn't do - at a time when they needed to preserve as many fans as possible.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They got away with it to a degree with 5th because they kept enough faithful and paid enough lipservice. Combined with the flagship status, some decent marketing and pop culture footprint allowed them to power through alienating a lot of people.<br /> That said they could have possibly done even better if they hadn't done that, it's not particularly clear why they think new players would not be interested in say paths or the actual Baali.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T13:15:30-07:00","id":1559535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559514#post1559514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God, I hope not. Everything from WoD5 gave me a bad taste in my mouth. Mage: The Ascension is my favorite World of Darkness gameline. I cannot imagine how awful a redux under Paradox's oversight would be.<br /> <br /> If M5 never happens, I'll be happy. Let's roll the dice that Paradox sells the property, and the next IP holder is more skittish about rocking the boat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <b>Princes of Darkness</b> mod for <i>CK3</i> has a better chance of revitalizing the franchise, than 5th edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T14:05:58-07:00","id":1559537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559519#post1559519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They got away with it to a degree with 5th because they kept enough faithful and paid enough lipservice. Combined with the flagship status, some decent marketing and pop culture footprint allowed them to power through alienating a lot of people.<br /> That said they could have possibly done even better if they hadn't done that, it's not particularly clear why they think new players would not be interested in say paths or the actual Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div>The people behind V5 pretty clearly didn't think that these things were a fit for their vision of a &quot;proper WoD&quot;. Hence, no matter how much interest, the only answer you were ever likely to get about whether or not they would show up would be a rude throwback to the 90s, when they were in the fandom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T17:50:53-07:00","id":1559539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559537#post1559537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The people behind V5 pretty clearly didn't think that these things were a fit for their vision of a &quot;proper WoD&quot;. Hence, no matter how much interest, the only answer you were ever likely to get about whether or not they would show up would be a rude throwback to the 90s, when they were in the fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods forbid that a game revolving around the concept of personal horror is allowed to be shocking and offensive.<br /> <br /> I've seen people describe the setting as a mixture of 'punk' and 'goth.'<br /> <br /> You know what punk and goth are most infamous for? Being radically counter culture!<br /> <br /> They rage against the machine, challenge societal norms, and call you slurs for trying to force them back in line.<br /> <br /> Punk and Goth are deliberately meant to invoke feelings of outrage. That's the whole fucking point!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T22:28:02-07:00","id":1559542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559537#post1559537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The people behind V5 pretty clearly didn't think that these things were a fit for their vision of a &quot;proper WoD&quot;. Hence, no matter how much interest, the only answer you were ever likely to get about whether or not they would show up would be a rude throwback to the 90s, when they were in the fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tricky part is the people behind v5 changed a lot this makes it hard to lock into whats planned. I suspect its confirmation bias that the more pretentious members/designers rationalize. <br /> <br /> We can see that the people actually running the show dont care about proper wod from them making a battle royale. Which raises further questions about why they dont like parts of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-20T23:58:18-07:00","id":1559543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559542#post1559542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tricky part is the people behind v5 changed a lot this makes it hard to lock into whats planned. I suspect its confirmation bias that the more pretentious members/designers rationalize.<br /> <br /> We can see that the people actually running the show dont care about proper wod from them making a battle royale. Which raises further questions about why they dont like parts of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>V5 Writers:</b> Camarilla are the bad guys!<br /> <br /> Recruits the Assamites and remodels them as a clan of vigilantes, who use their disciplines to punish evil doers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>V5 Writers:</b> Anarchs are the good guys!<br /> <br /> Recruits the Setites and Tzimisce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-21T17:39:21-07:00","id":1559553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559542#post1559542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tricky part is the people behind v5 changed a lot this makes it hard to lock into whats planned. I suspect its confirmation bias that the more pretentious members/designers rationalize.<br /> <br /> We can see that the people actually running the show dont care about proper wod from them making a battle royale. Which raises further questions about why they dont like parts of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the management proper doesn't love or hate it, except in as much as Bloodlines 2 underperformed and lost them money. They're the easiest part to figure out; they just want to make more money, and they do things with the IP that they think will do this.<br /> <br /> The TRPG folks at the White Wolf spinoff, though, have a vision. They're also former fans who are running the show according to what they liked or hated about the various games, and it's pretty obvious that they didn't like anything but Vampire, and even then, only a specific slice of Vampire. They do things like flattening all of the games to make them play more like Vampire, trimming out non-Vampire powers, and generally performing to all the appearances of being extremely... upset that anything ever upstaged Vampire in any arena.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods forbid that a game revolving around the concept of personal horror is allowed to be shocking and offensive.<br /> <br /> I've seen people describe the setting as a mixture of 'punk' and 'goth.'<br /> <br /> You know what punk and goth are most infamous for? Being radically counter culture!<br /> <br /> They rage against the machine, challenge societal norms, <b>and call you slurs for trying to force them back in line</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Rolls up a newspaper. Puts nails through it.)<br /> <br /> No. We're not doing that. Unless you somehow think that &quot;square&quot;, &quot;narc&quot; or the like constitutes a slur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Punk and Goth are deliberately meant to invoke feelings of outrage. That's the whole fucking point! </div> </div> </div>Every vampire main is like &quot;I want to be shocked and outraged!&quot;<br /> <br /> But then they enter a Werewolf crossover into the Splatter dimension and they're like &quot;Oh no, don't turn my awesome vampire character into dried-out, rotting mass of hamburger on the ground!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not even necessarily the Garou proper doing this. Plenty of fomori and other monsters are capable of it, by virtue of being physical threats on par with Garou. What's required for this makes them brutally overpowered to other games' main characters. Throwbacks from Freak Legion, for example, are terrible things for a neonate or an acolyte to run into, not unlike running into one of the ogre-like guards from Fear and Hunger. And if you know the other thing that the guards are infamous for... that actually tracks, too. Freak Legion has a power revolving around it!<br /> <br /> (Warning For the Uninitiated: Abandon all hope all ye who search for Freak Legion or Fear and Hunger.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-21T20:07:30-07:00","id":1559554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559553#post1559553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Rolls up a newspaper. Puts nails through it.)<br /> <br /> No. We're not doing that. Unless you somehow think that &quot;square&quot;, &quot;narc&quot; or the like constitutes a slur.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more referring to the F and R slurs. Which, as an autistic person growing up in the 90's period, I was constantly subjected to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559553#post1559553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every vampire main is like &quot;I want to be shocked and outraged!&quot;<br /> <br /> But then they enter a Werewolf crossover into the Splatter dimension and they're like &quot;Oh no, don't turn my awesome vampire character into dried-out, rotting mass of hamburger on the ground!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not even necessarily the Garou proper doing this. Plenty of fomori and other monsters are capable of it, by virtue of being physical threats on par with Garou. What's required for this makes them brutally overpowered to other games' main characters. Throwbacks from Freak Legion, for example, are terrible things for a neonate or an acolyte to run into, not unlike running into one of the ogre-like guards from Fear and Hunger. And if you know the other thing that the guards are infamous for... that actually tracks, too. Freak Legion has a power revolving around it!<br /> <br /> (Warning For the Uninitiated: Abandon all hope all ye who search for Freak Legion or Fear and Hunger.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean outrage in the sense of &quot;let's firebomb government buildings, tear down the corporations, and worship demons unironically.&quot; - Punks and Goths typically have a reputation for hating society, and wanting to see it all burn.<br /> <br /> I've heard about Freak Legion, but never actually seen any trace of its existence. People on Youtube seem to be too afraid to show any screen shots of it, in case their channels get demonetized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T07:56:45-07:00","id":1559562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559554#post1559554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've heard about Freak Legion, but never actually seen any trace of its existence. People on Youtube seem to be too afraid to show any screen shots of it, in case their channels get demonetized.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looks like The Primogen might have made a video covering it.<br /> <br /> Not sure if it's okay to link the video here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T08:06:52-07:00","id":1559563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do things like flattening all of the games to make them play more like Vampire, trimming out non-Vampire powers, and generally performing to all the appearances of being extremely... upset that anything ever upstaged Vampire in any arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage 1rst ed made a joke about how easy was for a mage with the rigth spheres to turn an Elder vampire into a lawnchair (and it wasn't THAT easy, it still needed Life 4 if I remember right. You can't have that from chargen).<br /> <br /> Mage did this joke <u><b>once</b></u><br /> <br /> Then on the Book of Shadows, also 1rst ed, has a disclaimer that, while it was feasible, turning an elder into a chair it's not something that you should ever do.<br /> <br /> And <i>even to this day</i>, after so much time have pass that most players have never actually read the original line, the Backlash of the &quot;Elder into Lawnchair&quot; it's still haunting us. With a whole section of M20 (on a book that did left many important rules off or unclear) <i>breaking the rules </i>or inventing new ones as to make sure it's not easy. Also telling you to never do it even if you can. <hr /><br /> And that on top of a whole plethora of rules to make other supernaturals, but vampires in particular, harder to affect. I.E: There's a penalizer to the difficulty to try and use Mind on a supernatural <i>,</i>+3 but it's +5 if they have Dominate or are an Elder Vampire, up to +8 if it's <i>also </i>forcing them against their will. (And unlike normal modifiers, these aren't limited to the maximum of +3 to the difficulty. Because &quot;you don't fuck with count dracula&quot; - the book actually says this) .<br /> <br /> Or my favorite: That you need special and incredibly prohibitive combination of Spheres to create &quot;<b>true sunlight</b>&quot; - <i>if it's even possible at all</i> (this last part it's from HDYDT, but rules to make sunligth harder to create predate M20). Because &quot;it's not the UV but a supernatural curse&quot;, or something. Curiously <i>&quot;<b>true</b> </i><b>silver&quot;</b> isn't <i>off limit</i> the way <i>sunlight</i> is, in spite of Shifters weaknesses <i>also </i>being supernatural in origin. I guess authors have more faith on Werewolves being able to<i> take it</i>. Or just don't care enough.<br /> <br /> On <i>Vampire</i>, the game where vampires are the protagonists and their Lore it's king, creating <i>true sunlight </i>it's just another normal Forces effect. <i>Vampire </i>doesn't feel the need to protect vamprire supremacy against mages as much as Mage does <hr /><br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can't wait fo M5 to double the bet, and say that nobody ever understood dynamic magic, so mages now have a streamlined set number of (not op, balanced with vampire) effects they can do at a cost, and maybe <i>some </i>form of more chaotic power that kills you if you use it even once. (And then declare it a <i>success </i>when on the playtest nobody chooses to use the dangerous dynamic magick option, just like they were so happy of how few Garou turned Crinos on a Werewolf playtest - well, fair it's fair, it would be appropiate: for a Mage game created by <i>Paradox, </i>the joke tells itself :P )<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But who knows? . I'm just a man on the internet inventing a fictional scenario and getting angry at it.<br /> <br /> Maybe M5 both happens, and becomes the black swan that surprises us as the best version of Mage ever.<br /> <br /> All I know after H5 it's that no cow it's sacred. If they were willing to erase the core splat of a gameline, we really can't expect Whilte Wolf to respect the <i>core premises</i> of the game if it goes against their vision. And given their vision as a street level angsty streamlined WoD, I'm not very hopefull","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-22-2026, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T09:22:30-07:00","id":1559566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559563#post1559563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mage 1rst ed made a joke about how easy was for a mage with the rigth spheres to turn an Elder vampire into a lawnchair (and it wasn't THAT easy, it still needed Life 4 if I remember right. You can't have that from chargen).<br /> <br /> Mage did this joke <u><b>once</b></u><br /> <br /> Then on the Book of Shadows, also 1rst ed, has a disclaimer that, while it was feasible, turning an elder into a chair it's not something that you should ever do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Tzimisce do it for fun!<br /> <br /> Also, turning people into chairs or summoning true sunlight may be difficult to achieve.<br /> <br /> You know what's not difficult, though?<br /> <br /> <b>FIREBALL!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 04-22-2026, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T13:33:14-07:00","id":1559571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559554#post1559554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was more referring to the F and R slurs. Which, as an autistic person growing up in the 90's period, I was constantly subjected to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in those days, that was basically the default for Toxic Male Dialogue with &quot;Friends&quot;. So it'd be difficult to see any kind of clarion involving picking that cursed sword back up as anything other than a return to the insecure, homophobic*, able-ist days of my middle school youth. And to then hate it, because it was terrible.<br /> <br /> *Everything-phobic, really, but it got compacted for visiblity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean outrage in the sense of &quot;let's firebomb government buildings, tear down the corporations, and worship demons unironically.&quot; - Punks and Goths typically have a reputation for hating society, and wanting to see it all burn. </div> </div> </div>Well, given that a number of regrettably influential strains of Christianity declare everything to be demonic on the reg, &quot;worship demons unironically&quot; frequently just means not being a Christian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've heard about Freak Legion, but never actually seen any trace of its existence. People on Youtube seem to be too afraid to show any screen shots of it, in case their channels get demonetized. </div> </div> </div>There are like a dozen copies on ebay, and the ebook is only five bucks or so on DTRPG if you don't want to buy it for the 1995 cost adjusted for inflation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage 1rst ed made a joke about how easy was for a mage with the rigth spheres to turn an Elder vampire into a lawnchair (and it wasn't THAT easy, it still needed Life 4 if I remember right. You can't have that from chargen).<br /> <br /> Mage did this joke <u><b>once</b></u><br /> <br /> Then on the Book of Shadows, also 1rst ed, has a disclaimer that, while it was feasible, turning an elder into a chair it's not something that you should ever do.<br /> <br /> And <i>even to this day</i>, after so much time have pass that most players have never actually read the original line, the Backlash of the &quot;Elder into Lawnchair&quot; it's still haunting us. With a whole section of M20 (on a book that did left many important rules off or unclear) <i>breaking the rules </i>or inventing new ones as to make sure it's not easy. Also telling you to never do it even if you can.<br /> <br /> And that on top of a whole plethora of rules to make other supernaturals, but vampires in particular, harder to affect. I.E: There's a penalizer to the difficulty to try and use Mind on a supernatural <i>,</i>+3 but it's +5 if they have Dominate or are an Elder Vampire, up to +8 if it's <i>also </i>forcing them against their will. (And unlike normal modifiers, these aren't limited to the maximum of +3 to the difficulty. Because &quot;you don't fuck with count dracula&quot; - the book actually says this) .<br /> <br /> Or my favorite: That you need special and incredibly prohibitive combination of Spheres to create &quot;<b>true sunlight</b>&quot; - <i>if it's even possible at all</i> (this last part it's from HDYDT, but rules to make sunligth harder to create predate M20). Because &quot;it's not the UV but a supernatural curse&quot;, or something. Curiously <i>&quot;<b>true</b> </i><b>silver&quot;</b> isn't <i>off limit</i> the way <i>sunlight</i> is, in spite of Shifters weaknesses <i>also </i>being supernatural in origin. I guess authors have more faith on Werewolves being able to<i> take it</i>. Or just don't care enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess would be more that they don't care, though it might also protect mages in some respect, because there's a gift to sense it, which is in-splat for Ahrouns, so you might end up giving yourself away to the worst possibly observer if you use Matter to make it or turn something else into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On <i>Vampire</i>, the game where vampires are the protagonists and their Lore it's king, creating <i>true sunlight </i>it's just another normal Forces effect. <i>Vampire </i>doesn't feel the need to protect vamprire supremacy against mages as much as Mage does </div> </div> </div>Antagonist designation can be like that. Keep in mind that Lupines in V:tM are defined with Disciplines and have Potence (auto-successes until V20) instead of a dice pool bonus to Strength. And don't really have any of the cool, weird shit that Garou do, like Phone Travel/Signal Rider or Jam Technology.<br /> <br /> [quote]<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I can't wait fo M5 to double the bet, and say that nobody ever understood dynamic magic, so mages now have a streamlined set number of (not op, balanced with vampire) effects they can do at a cost, and maybe <i>some </i>form of more chaotic power that kills you if you use it even once. (And then declare it a <i>success </i>when on the playtest nobody chooses to use the dangerous dynamic magick option, just like they were so happy of how few Garou turned Crinos on a Werewolf playtest - well, fair it's fair, it would be appropiate: for a Mage game created by <i>Paradox, </i>the joke tells itself :P )<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> [quote]<br /> <br /> &quot;Who wrote this?&quot;<br /> <br /> [Zoom out of panel to see a smiling Wrinkle holding a cartoonist's pen]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But who knows? . I'm just a man on the internet inventing a fictional scenario and getting angry at it.<br /> <br /> Maybe M5 both happens, and becomes the black swan that surprises us as the best version of Mage ever.<br /> <br /> All I know after H5 it's that no cow it's sacred. If they were willing to erase the core splat of a gameline, we really can't expect Whilte Wolf to respect the <i>core premises</i> of the game if it goes against their vision. And given their vision as a street level angsty streamlined WoD, I'm not very hopefull\u200b </div> </div> </div>&quot;If you want to picture the future, imagine Destiny's Price defining everything about your game - forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> No one is hopeful. That's why everyone makes grim jokes, kind of like the anime fandom in the oughties to mid-teens, where the prospect of 4Kids trying to localize a series clearly not meant for kids was both hilarious but also discouraging because it could technically happen. Here, though... the &quot;could&quot; changed to &quot;will&quot;, as it's already happened. W5 is like someone <i>actually made</i> the &quot;Casey and Friends&quot; or &quot;Bully La Bully&quot; version of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> So for Mage, it's kind of like the imminent appearance of &quot;Disappear Note&quot; or &quot;The Melancholy of Harriet Susan Myers&quot;. I don't even think they're going to try making Changeling, since they can technically teleport a vampire into an Upeo Death Drop, or possibly even to the moon, with Wayfare 1.\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T13:57:37-07:00","id":1559572,"title":"","content":"The weird part about the 20 year temper tantrum about the lawn chair is that is did nothing to limit how easy it is to kill a vampire with something as simple as forces 3, prime 2 which instantly turns a vampire into a blowtorch.<br /> <br /> Combined with mind and m20 rules meaning roughly 50% of disciplines dont work very well on mages and the lawn chair gripe becomes absurd. if anything if you can do that you've already won and are just showboating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T15:41:24-07:00","id":1559573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559566#post1559566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also, turning people into chairs or summoning true sunlight may be difficult to achieve.<br /> <br /> You know what's not difficult, though?<br /> <br /> <b>FIREBALL!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Have a blast! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T19:02:11-07:00","id":1559575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559572#post1559572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird part about the 20 year temper tantrum about the lawn chair is that is did nothing to limit how easy it is to kill a vampire with something as simple as forces 3, prime 2 which instantly turns a vampire into a blowtorch.<br /> <br /> Combined with mind and m20 rules meaning roughly 50% of disciplines dont work very well on mages and the lawn chair gripe becomes absurd. if anything if you can do that you've already won and are just showboating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternately, Matter/Correspondence and/or Forces.<br /> <br /> &quot;What are you going to do with that staff, Gandalf?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The floor is lava!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;ARGH IT BURNS!&quot;<br /> <br /> (Alternately, the floor is thermite. A nice, deep pit of thermite that Forces can easily ignite.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T19:36:01-07:00","id":1559576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559563#post1559563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With a whole section of M20 (on a book that did left many important rules off or unclear) <i>breaking the rules </i>or inventing new ones as to make sure it's not easy. Also telling you to never do it even if you can.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is not an exaggeration. I count at least 4 rule breaks or invented mechanics. Three for mages, at least 1 for vampires.<br /> <br /> For mages this:<br /> <br /> - Suspends normal Vulgarity rules. It is always Vulgar even in the mage\u2019s sanctum<br /> <br /> - Increases Matter requirements to 5 because, glibly, \u201cvampires aren\u2019t on the periodic table of elements.\u201d<br /> <br /> - Requires enough extra successes to drop the vampire to incapacitated, which is not a thing any other transformation spell does.<br /> <br /> For vampires:<br /> <br /> -Frenzied vampires with any blood in the pool can burn it all to change back. Coincidentally, being turned into a lawn chair prompts a difficulty 8 frenzy roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When you have to add that many invented mechanics to stop the spell from working, you basically prove it works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T09:12:06-07:00","id":1559583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559346-is-mage-5th-edition-going-to-happen?p=1559572#post1559572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The weird part about the 20 year temper tantrum about the lawn chair is that is did nothing to limit how easy it is to kill a vampire with something as simple as forces 3, prime 2 which instantly turns a vampire into a blowtorch.<br /> <br /> Combined with mind and m20 rules meaning roughly 50% of disciplines dont work very well on mages and the lawn chair gripe becomes absurd. if anything if you can do that you've already won and are just showboating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all this overcorrecting and they ALSO miss the point.<br /> <br /> But to be fair, mages and vampires aren't <i>easy</i> to balance on a traditional RPG way - they sort of work past each other rules wise. And I can't say I have <i>the solution</i>, but punishing one or two maligned Effects sure ain't it.<br /> <br /> In a sense, it boils down to the narratives of the games. Vampire sort of wants you to have no recourse against the Elders, so it chains your character and forces to think outside the magic box if you want to find solutions to your immortal problems. You're expected to be submisive towards the Elders 'til they lower their guard.<br /> <br /> Mage stance on authority it's about freedom with consequences, they're not made to wait a hundred years plotting under the wing of some schmoc - even if that can potentialy happen. The infamous story of the Elder into Lawnchair it's, if nothing else, <i>symbolic </i>of that divide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-23T10:18:43-07:00","id":1559584,"title":"","content":"It also may be Brucato's personal grudge. I can't actually speak to his motivations, but this isn't the only point where M20 starts inventing mechanics to make something difficult. The Transposing Locations section of HDYDT also invents its own success requirements (which starts at 20 for even the smallest, shortest application, and the example used takes 70+), invents its own Paradox rules (based on duration), bans the use of all spell modifiers, and includes at least two incidents of snark (&quot;Such things make Storytellers (and game designers) seek out other lines of work.&quot;).<br /> <br /> I have no idea his actual feelings on the two sections, but it is hard not to read active hostility out of them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}